  - permutation test
  - fluctuation test
  - subgroup analysis
  - machine learning
abstract: >-
  FairTree is a Python package for subgroup fairness auditing of machine
  learning models. It scans covariates of mixed type (continuous,
  ordinal, binary, unordered categorical) for subgroups where model
  prediction error changes systematically, distinguishing shifts in bias
  from shifts in variance. Two statistical variants are provided: a
  score-based fluctuation test using the Brownian bridge, and a
  non-parametric permutation test with proper maximally-selected
  statistic correction.
